---
import ProseLayout from '../../layouts/ProseLayout.astro';
import { DEMO_BOOKING_URL, CONTACT_EMAIL, contactMailto } from '../../config';
---
<ProseLayout
  title="Privacy information"
  metaTitle="Privacy | PumpOS"
  description="What PumpOS collects, who handles it, and how to ask us about your data."
  path="/legal/privacy"
  eyebrow="PumpOS pilot"
  legal
>
  <p slot="meta" class="legal-updated">Last updated 20 October 2026. We update this page when PumpOS or the way we handle data changes.</p>

  <h2>Who runs PumpOS</h2>
  <p>PumpOS is run by Abdullah Nettoor from Kochi, Kerala, India. Write to <a href={contactMailto('Privacy question')}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> with any privacy question.</p>

  <h2>Demos</h2>
  {DEMO_BOOKING_URL ? (
    <p>The demo form sends your name, phone number, station name and town, and any tank, nozzle and attendant counts you enter, to our booking calendar so you can choose a time.</p>
  ) : (
    <p>The demo form does not send anything to our servers. It opens WhatsApp with a message to us containing your name, phone number, station name and town, and any tank, nozzle and attendant counts you entered. Nothing reaches us until you press send. You can also write to us at {CONTACT_EMAIL} instead.</p>
  )}
  <p>If you message us on WhatsApp, WhatsApp (Meta) carries the conversation and your number. The WhatsApp links on this site go through our own <code>/whatsapp</code> page, which only forwards you to WhatsApp.</p>
  <p>We use what you send to reply, arrange the demo and talk about the pilot. Please don't send customer lists, bank statements or other records. The demo uses sample data.</p>
  <p>For a hands-on demo we may create a sample station filled with sample data. If you give us an email address, PumpOS sends you a sign-in invitation for that station. Each demo has an expiry date that we set when we create it. On that date its logins stop working. Seven days later PumpOS deletes the demo organisation, its sample records and its logins. We can extend a demo if you ask.</p>

  <h2>Pilot stations</h2>
  <p>Once a station joins the pilot, its team enters operational records into PumpOS: shifts, nozzle readings, sales, stock, collections, expenses and credit customers. These records include personal details that the station chooses to add, such as staff names, phone numbers and email addresses, and the names and contact details of its credit customers.</p>
  <p>Each organisation's records are kept apart from every other organisation's. Inside an organisation, the role the owner gives each user decides what that user can see and do. We access a station's records only when needed to set up or support it.</p>
  <p>The station decides how the staff and customer details it enters are used. PumpOS stores and processes them on the station's behalf, to run the service for that station.</p>

  <h2>Providers that handle data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Cloudflare.</strong> Hosts this website, the web console, the mobile web app and the PumpOS API, and connects the API to the database. When you visit this website, Cloudflare receives your IP address and browser details to deliver the page. This site sets no cookies and loads no tracking scripts. Cloudflare also keeps a sample of API request logs, which can include IP addresses, so we can find and fix errors. Only we can see them.</li>
    <li><strong>Supabase.</strong> Hosts the database that holds station records, and runs sign-in, including the sign-in invitation emails.</li>
    <li><strong>GitHub.</strong> Serves the desktop app download and its update checks. Each check sends GitHub a normal web request from your computer.</li>
    <li><strong>Google (Gmail).</strong> Receives email sent to {CONTACT_EMAIL}.</li>
    <li><strong>WhatsApp (Meta).</strong> Only if you message us there.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The database is in Supabase's Mumbai region, in India. The other providers may process data outside India. We make no claim about certifications or compliance standards.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Demo stations: deleted seven days after the demo expires.</li>
    <li>Pilot station records: kept while your organisation uses PumpOS. On request, we send you a copy of your station's records. If you ask us to delete them, we delete them within 30 days.</li>
    <li>Demo requests by email or WhatsApp: deleted when you ask us to.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your requests</h2>
  <p>To see, correct or delete information you have sent us, email <a href={contactMailto('Privacy request')}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. If you work at a pilot station, ask your station's owner first: they control the records your station keeps in PumpOS. We reply within 14 days.</p>
  <p>Grievance contact: Abdullah Nettoor, <a href={contactMailto('Privacy grievance')}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
</ProseLayout>
